sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) up-the-gradient PIN1 polarization with explicit PIN1 trafficking kinetics, quasi-3D subepidermal canalization, and polar auxin transport for shoot apical meristem phyllotaxis faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermis & subepidermal provascular strand); Aeonium tabuliforme (spiral rosette specimen) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermis & subepidermal provascular strand); Aeonium tabuliforme (spiral rosette specimen) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 75.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-auxin-pin1-phyllotaxis-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py; output: docs/media/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermis & subepidermal provascular strand); Aeonium tabuliforme (spiral rosette specimen); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 4bb87fc40e78808765bf8caaa78c3f40f08c88fe6ce9f43531ffe4997786d304; artifact_sha256: 2b06a6ed998e8eaa0669c12d96a5cab8df703b0a27180f87a7433246768cfcb9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis_reference.json=b0ad3fb44bd3bd21..., datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=5585fae958a7d7ee..., datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/rosette_phyllotaxis_specimen.jpg=ec50801b52dabc46..., datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/scout_manifest.json=2e474ee5544f04f4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-auxin-pin1-phyllotaxis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1633-1638 & Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1301-1306: up-the-gradient PIN1 membrane allocation P_ij = P_i exp(c_1 a_j) / sum_k exp(c_1 a_k) with explicit PIN1 membrane cycling kinetics whose quasi-steady state is that allocation, intercellular active polar + diffusive auxin transport, and periodic convergence maxima separated by a characteristic wavelength | Geldner et al. (2001) Nature: brefeldin A blocks PIN1 exocytosis and internalises plasma-membrane PIN1 within 1-2 h; Paciorek et al. (2005) Nature: auxin inhibits PIN endocytosis | Bayer et al. (2009) Genes Dev: epidermal up-the-gradient patterning couples to subepidermal with-the-flux canalization (Mitchison 1980/1981; Feugier et al. 2005) producing a narrow provascular strand from the L1 convergence point to the existing vasculature; Scarpella et al. (2006): PIN1-marked preprocambial strands are 1-2 cells wide | Smith et al. (2006): transitions across spiral (137.5 deg), distichous (180 deg), decussate (90 deg) and tricussate (120 deg) phyllotaxis with meristem size; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature: NPA/pin1 pin-formed apex and localized IAA rescue; reconstructed_in_script: Explicit per-cell cytosolic + per-wall membrane PIN1 pools cycling by first-order exocytosis (targeting f_ij = exp(c_1 (a_j - a_0))) and endocytosis, solved by an exact exponential integrator (membrane + cytosol conservation err 0.0, flux antisymmetry err 1.3e-14), with QSS ablation, BFA block (PM fraction 0.0857 after 2 h = PM(t_BFA) exp(-k_endo 2 h) exactly; polarity 0.052 vs WT 0.584), auxin-inhibited-endocytosis variant (polarity 0.21) and fast-cycling Boltzmann limit (max |P - Boltzmann| 0.013) | Quasi-3D 15 x 12 subepidermal slice beneath P1 with with-the-flux Hill feedback f_ij = f_0 + J^n/(K^n + J^n): single-file strand (width 1 cell at mid-depth, mean 1.0 over rows 1-8, flux concentration 0.63, 97 % of source flux delivered to the sink); no-feedback ablation width 14 cells; Hill-exponent sweep widths {15, 6, 1, 1, 1} for n in {1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3} (Spearman rho -0.89, p 0.04) | Linearized Turing-like dispersion relation with kappa_4 calibrated so that the peak sits at the 5.2-cell reference (threshold c_1 a_0 = 1.75; NPA collapse sigma(k) < 0); 1D ring NPA (contrast 1.000, 0 peaks) and IAA-paste rescue (1 peak at 60 deg) | ExG + DoG segmentation of 410 leaf tips on the SHA-256-locked Aeonium tabuliforme rosette (12/12 sectors, NN 1 - CV = 0.774); transfer_boundary: The 180-cell dome does NOT generate its primordia: P1..P8 are seeded at golden-angle targets (L396-397) and the auxin field is relaxed toward a prescribed envelope (L508-513); only the PIN1 trafficking, polarity, conservation and BFA/QSS/fast-cycling results are emergent outputs of that function | The four phyllotactic regimes are prescribed (nominal angle + seeded noise, L944-957; spiral placed at k*137.5 deg, L923-931) and the WT ring profile is hand-built (L1025-1028); Gamma is a label, not a control parameter | The canalization model is one non-growing vertical slice with a uniform Dirichlet sink row, no lateral neighbours' strands, no growth and no 3D geometry; strand width is compared to a literature band (1-2 cells), not to a vendored PIN1::GFP image | The rosette specimen is Aeonium tabuliforme (top-down leaf rosette), not an Arabidopsis inflorescence meristem; does_not_claim: Full 3D meristem geometry, tissue growth or cell division, PIN1 phosphorylation (PINOID/PP2A) control of apical-basal targeting, emergent golden-angle phyllotaxis, emergent mode transitions with Gamma, or a quantitative comparison of PIN1 plasma-membrane fractions with immunolocalization data]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.759"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
